  "result": "The fix is in `src/lib/event-bus.ts`. Detaching a handler now removes it from the set that is live at detach time, not from the copy captured at attach time. Before, once a second handler subscribed to the same event type, the first handler's detach silently did nothing, so each detach/re-attach cycle stacked another copy of the audit, usage and search handlers.\n\nI added regression tests to `tests/lib/event-bus.test.ts` and a new `tests/server/event-registry.test.ts` that drives attach/detach/re-attach cycles through the real registry. The full suite passes (74 files, 622 tests), and typecheck and lint are clean.\n\nOne thing doesn't fully match the report: in this registration order the webhook handler is the last subscriber for `issue.created` and `issue.status_changed`, so the old bug alone didn't stack webhook copies in my reproduction. The fix removes duplication for any order, but if webhook duplicates still show up in production, the cause is somewhere else in the delivery path.",
